# Adopt the selected knowledge lifecycle

This pinned target guide replaces global bookkeeping with producing-role handover, selected
qualification, current knowledge use and the existing PTTC close. It introduces no runtime,
portfolio queue, task reopening, retrospective, new authority or automatic fact conversion.
Published release routing names this guide from its version-addressed entry; an authorized untagged
target is identified by its actual full commit, never a future tag or version.

## 1. Resolve source, authority and prerequisite

Use the final verified target's update workflow and this guide, including equal-version updates and
incomplete attempts. Resolve exact target SHA/guide bytes, current provenance, receiver update authority,
selected adapters and existing preservation/attempt receipts before an already-current return.
Unknown/custom upstream routes or contradictory provenance need their existing project-specific
authority. Do not use init, a live source tree or a guessed before-image to repair an update.

An incomplete SLC 3.3.0 connected group must first complete or refuse under the same target's
[3.3.0 guide](3.3.0.md): exact active/history choices, disposition/membership, preserved historical
digest pairs and expected cuts remain its rule. TKL cannot bypass/reset that group or turn later
state into an old snapshot. A completed SLC receiver needs no repeat historical sweep for TKL.
Retain ordinary active discovery and deduplicated active/history exact-reference union, whole-ID
collision refusal and custom container choices. TKL changes none of these fields.

## 2. Account for functions and bounded effects

| Existing function/setting | Successor or preserved meaning |
|---|---|
| Architecture map, important artifacts, legacy replacements | Retain useful `KNOWLEDGE.md` ranges and their source links; update only affected entry/reference prose |
| Legacy D decisions and category/F facts | Preserve rows, meaning, source URLs/paths and identities; no mass conversion |
| New human knowledge / technical decisions | Independent records, same form, existing knowledge/docs owners; actual acceptance still required |
| Producing-role insights | Existing role/stage source first; minimal task-local fallback only when necessary |
| Currentness and conflict | Scope/source/disposition plus incoming relations to exact record or legacy identity/epoch |
| `tfw.knowledge.interval`, `gate_mode` | Retire live numeric planning gate; selected material handover/use/close obligations replace it |
| `max_facts_per_topic`, `max_topic_files`, obsolete `max_index_lines` | Retire maintained inventory/size limits, no numeric replacement |
| `KNOWLEDGE.md` fact counts/list of every record | Remove only maintained counts/inventory instructions; retain directory/category/source routes and all non-count meaning |
| Existing `.tfw/knowledge_state.yaml` and processed markers | Preserve exact bytes as inert historical evidence, no newly processed IDs or consolidation claim |
| Fresh knowledge-state template | Remove framework scaffold from new payload; fresh init creates no state file |
| Optional old `knowledge-pending` diagnostic | Reports retirement and the selected route without corpus/state reading |

Unknown custom keys or receiver-purpose text are not silently removed. Preserve them and resolve
their exact function through existing authority. Remove an empty `tfw.knowledge` map only after its
listed retired children are removed; unrelated config, configured checks, profiles/grants, private
preferences, topic/source bytes, markers and task/control history remain untouched.

## 3. Preserve before affected writes

Create an immutable content-addressed before-image within the existing `.tfw/update_receipts/`
mechanism before any affected config/entry/provenance change. Include exact target/guide identity,
actual authority, old/intended fields with explicit absence, complete original config/entry/state
bytes (including absent state), retained topic/source hashes, and selected compatible-reader/adapter
paths with old/intended identities. The intended entry edit preserves legacy rows and source links.
This finite attachment is evidence, never a mutable inventory or receiver runtime state.

Use existing attachment bytes when their content address agrees; refuse a same-address mismatch.
Do not place secrets or private preferences in an attachment. For self-adoption before Candidate,
bind the actual immutable Baseline and TS approval plus proposed payload/guide hashes; later evidence
binds the tested Candidate. Never write a predicted Candidate SHA into a before-image.

## 4. Apply compatible readers, then retire live authority

At a safe boundary for affected writers, use semantic YAML support available to the agent; receivers
need no shipped executable/Python service. Reject duplicate/malformed YAML keys and ambiguous fields.

1. Install the selected compatible canonical capture/qualification/use/close readers, record and
   fallback forms, and exact selected adapter copies. Enable both legacy and new-record reads before
   retiring the old gate/setting authority. Do not install unselected provider roots.
2. Immediately before each affected write, re-read actual source/authority and preserved old/intended
   fields/reader identities. Continue only from an expected old or intended value. A third value,
   missing preservation, conflicting source or authority stops the connected affected operation.
3. Merge only the named config retirements and stable `KNOWLEDGE.md` entry/count-instruction changes.
   Preserve project-specific fields and all legacy D/F meaning. Preserve old knowledge-state and
   markers byte-for-byte; state absence stays absence. New accepted records require their own actual
   qualification decision, never update permission alone. No upstream project/team/knowledge memory.
4. Verify actual compatible reader/copy effects, config/entry values, source links and retained bytes
   before provenance completion. Keep ordinary receiver checks; upstream pytest/MkDocs is not a
   receiver prerequisite. Complete cleanup disposition, immutable attempt receipt and outcome in the
   update workflow's existing order. Distinguish prepared, applied, checked and published effects.

These are recoverable sequential effects, not an atomic transaction across arbitrary readers.
Failures preserve current input and every original attempt. Never restore an entire old map or tree.

## 5. Re-enter expected cuts or refuse later state

Resolve the same pinned target and original preservation. Re-observe actual affected fields and
compatible-reader identities; old/intended cuts may continue. Validate unrelated later changes stay
untouched. A changed affected field requires its own authoritative decision, not a rollback.

| Actual observed cut | Bounded next action |
|---|---|
| No preservation, no affected write | Observe and preserve before application |
| Preservation only | Verify and reuse attachment; enable compatible readers/adapters |
| Readers only | Verify them; revalidate old fields before config/entry changes |
| Some config/entry fields intended, others old | Verify each affected field independently, complete only missing effects |
| Effects complete, provenance/receipt/outcome incomplete | Verify actual result, finish only remaining update obligations |
| Identical completed repeat, including equal version | Verify effects/applicability/receipt and report unchanged, no publication/inventory write or repeat question |
| Source/authority diverges, preservation missing/collides, affected field is Z | Refuse the connected operation; preserve Z and unrelated later work; name conflict and next owner action |
| Incomplete SLC group or conflicting established history | Return to its pinned original recovery/refusal route before any TKL effect |

Prepared cuts are labelled prepared, never observed crashes. A record or receipt is not authority
over later changes. Legacy readers/history remain inspectable; current consumers use the compatible
contract, not old counters. Keep prior guides, sources and acceptance epochs unchanged.

## 6. Verify and explain

Check clean init and established/self receivers separately: stable entry/forms, no new state scaffold
or upstream memory; retained topics/D/source links and inert state; selected adapters including their
generated copies; unchanged completed repeat; concrete later-field refusal. Confirm source and
compiled routes independently where the receiver actually compiles documentation.
Record actual target, before-images, changed/preserved paths, observed outcomes, limitations and next
action in the existing receipt. File/model checks do not establish native behavior, publication or
owner comprehension. No historical task is reopened, silently completed or newly consolidated.
